{title: Calling On The Name}
{subtitle: Genesis 4:26; 5:6; 5:9–10; Luke 3:38}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [F/A] | [Gm] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Seth lived one hundred and [F/A]five
[Gm]Then he saw a son ar[Eb]rive
[Bb]He named him Enosh, [F/A]pure and true [Gm]
[Eb]Into the line where faith [Fsus4]grew [F]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]At that time the people [F]found
[Dm]A way to make their hearts [Gm]sound
[Eb]They began to call a[F]loud
On the name of the [Bb]Lord [Eb/Bb]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]When Enosh was ninety years [F/A]old
[Gm]He fathered Kenan, as [Eb]told
[Bb]Eight hundred and fifteen [F/A]more
He lived, [Eb]keeping faith to the [F]core
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Eb]Other sons and daughters [F]came
[Dm7]In the name they bore the [Gm]same
[Eb]From Adam down to Seth’s [F]line
Enosh stands in grace di[Bb]vine [Eb/Bb]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Eb]Luke lists him in the [F]chain
[Dm7]The son of Enosh, plain and [Gm]plain
[Eb]Son of Seth, son of Adam’s [F]seed
From God, the story is [Bb]read [Eb]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Calling on the name of the [Bb]Lord
{end_of_verse}

